  annote  = {Book-length treatment of the measure embedding, and the only source here
             that develops it as a linear-programming theory rather than as
             machinery for a hierarchy. Ch1 section 4 "Metamorphosis" is the
             embedding itself; Ch2 existence and the weak-star topology; Ch3
             "Linear programs" sections 2-3 the finite-dimensional truncation
             and its approximation properties; Ch4 approximations; Ch6
             controllability; Appendix sections 3-4 functionals, measures, and
             the minimum of a linear form at an extremal point. Useful for the
             Paper 1 background section: it predates moment-SOS entirely, so it
             separates what is intrinsic to the embedding from what is an
             artifact of the SDP. Full text greppable in the MinerU markdown.},
}

