             m - n auxiliary variables come with constraints, of the algebraic
             form phi_k(X) = 0 and the product form X_i X_j = Z_i, and the
             constraint set is INVARIANT UNDER THE FLOW of the recast system
             because the initial conditions satisfy it. That is exactly the
             forward-invariance obligation apx:embedding incurs when it adds
             auxiliary states, discharged here in general form; the recast
             trajectory stays on a manifold of the ORIGINAL dimension, so the
             lift adds coordinates without adding dynamics. Corollaries 1-3
             pp94-95 extend to higher-order, implicit, delay and
