             LIGHTHILL'S THIRD-ORDER relation, cubic. So carrying first-order
             piston theory costs nothing in degree, and each further order costs
             one degree in the downwash, which is itself linear in the modal
             rates --- so second order takes the modal block to degree two and
             third order to degree three, multiplying through the Gram basis.
